I added a check at the top of `takeBack` that returns 0 before anything is changed when the loan's latest log entry is a `"back"` of the same kind, day and minute. Counts are not compared, and an empty log is never a repeat.

I couldn't see `record`, so I assumed it appends new entries to the end of `loan.log`. If it puts them at the front, the check should read `loan.log[0]` instead.
